---
import EssencePlanner from "@/components/EssencePlanner";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Essence Planner"
  wide
  description="Army-level essence planner for Songs of Conquest — fill your troop slots, add your wielder's magic skills, and see which spells you can actually cast and how often."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Essence Planner</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 mb-6 max-w-3xl text-muted-foreground">
    Every other score on this site rates one stack alone. Essence doesn't work
    that way: a stack generates its essence <em>once per round</em> no matter
    how many troops are in it, the whole army pools it, and spells draw from
    that pool at fixed costs. Fill your slots, set your wielder's magic skills,
    and this answers the question the per-unit numbers can't.
  </p>

  <EssencePlanner client:load />

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
    <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold">Why essence needs its own view</h2>
    <p>
      <strong class="text-foreground">Essence value is a step function, not a line.</strong>
      Chain Lightning costs 12 Chaos. Going from 10 a round to 12 turns it from
      a spell you cast every other round into one you cast every round; going
      from 12 to 14 does nothing at all until the next threshold. The{" "}
      <a class="underline hover:text-gold" href="/compare/">compare table</a>'s
      Magic score prices essence linearly, because a per-unit number has no way
      to know which threshold you're reaching for. That's what this page is for.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong class="text-foreground">It's per stack, not per troop.</strong>
      Five Faey Spirits generate exactly what twenty do. So a cheap unit with
      two essence is a better battery per gold than an expensive one with two,
      and the binding constraint is troop slots rather than gold. That's the
      reasoning behind spamming cheap generators, and it's why the Efficiency
      column alone will never recommend it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong class="text-foreground">A school's magic skill is a gate, not just income.</strong>
      Every level grants the same essence a round; what the levels buy is the
      spell tier. Chaos Magic 3 is what turns Chain Lightning's 35 damage into
      100, so the skill matters twice over, and a dyad spell needs both of its
      schools and casts at the lower of the two.
    </p>
    <p class="border-l-2 border-border pl-3">
      <strong class="text-foreground">Assumptions:</strong> troops generate
      their essence at the start of every round and the pool starts empty, so
      the first cast lands on turn ⌈cost ÷ income⌉. Charge Essence is modelled
      as doubling that stack's output on rounds you fire it, which costs the
      stack its turn — a trade this page doesn't price. Slot count is a control
      rather than a fixed 6, since army capacity varies. Not modelled: Essence
      Burst and other opening bonuses, Essence Leech from kills, Symbiosis
      auras, artifacts, or spending essence on anything but the spell you're
      looking at.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
